<title>GERMANY: Thyssen wins Indonesia contract.</title>
<headline>Thyssen wins Indonesia contract.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thyssen AG and Ferrostaal AG, with Indonesian shipyard PT PAL, have won a 182 million mark ($120.3 million) contract to supply parts for five container ships, Thyssen said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Under a contract signed during Chancellor Helmut Kohl's visit to Indonesia, the group will supply the parts to state owned Reederei PT Jakarta Lloyd, Thyssen said in a statement.</p>
<p>Project financing will be backed by Germany's Creditanstalt fuer Wiederaufbau. ($1=1.5130 Mark)</p>
